# 124 - aegis-fullscreen (user feedback 2026-11-13: "why it is still showing
# google header with address bar ... I told you I want full screen chrome
# therefore we used dock and after that you still didn't remove its")
# Patch 080 hid the top control container once during startup, but the
# browser-controls machinery re-shows it, so content pages still had the
# classic top toolbar (screenshot r70 device: URL bar + home/new-tab/tabs/
# menu at the top while the dock floats at the bottom). This patch makes the
# removal permanent: a chrome_java helper hides the container (and the
# bottom controls host), re-asserts the hidden state every second, and
# ToolbarControlContainer reports a zero top-controls height so nothing is
# reserved above the page. The dock URL pill is the address line.

